The cause of terrorist acts such as these is not a collective madness, religious fanaticism[ or] "cowardice",[ but] cold rational reflection[ by] small[ numbers of exceptionally] agg[rieved and alienated] people who[ are] driven to desperation by perceived chronic injustices[ to] which they[ can see] no peaceable solution.
To really put an end to such acts, in addition to[ finding], arresting, prosecuting and incarcer[ating] such people, we have got to tighten our belts and open our minds and hearts.
We need to pay a whole lot more attention to the terrible things that are happening day[ by] day[ to people] around the world than we have been in the habit of doing up to now; and we must join more wholeheartedly in the world-wide effort to eliminate human suffering and inequity, and broaden the realm of justice[.]
